0..74 Comment "//! A type calls a module\'s function through the module\'s name, as a value"
75..84 Comment "//! does."
85..88 Comment "//!"
89..165 Comment "//! A theory states its types as functions to `Type`, and a model calls them"
166..242 Comment "//! through the module that declares them. The printer writes such a type as"
243..307 Comment "//! that call. So the type must read back as the call it prints."
308..311 Comment "//!"
312..389 Comment "//! `Standard.same(Integer)` calls the function and decodes the code that the"
390..466 Comment "//! call returns. `Standard.unit()` runs a function of no input: a qualified"
467..545 Comment "//! link ends at a value name only before a list, so the empty list stands for"
546..593 Comment "//! the bare name. `Standard.after(Integer)(n)`"
594..667 Comment "//! applies the call\'s result to one more argument. A second list after a"
668..727 Comment "//! type family is not a call, and the lowering refuses it."
728..731 Comment "//!"
732..803 Comment "//! - see: #5213 — a type reads a qualified call and a call of a call"
